  "slug": "scientific-fair-5429",
  "summary": "New methods separate heritable from microenvironmental effects and enumerate metastatic migration histories, making inferential ambiguity explicit.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is inferring history, inheritance and structure from static or imaging-based measurements with explicit statistical models. MACH2 enumerates all optimal metastatic migration histories from DNA sequencing and adds a clone-location parsimony criterion, characterizing the solution space. SOUR separates heritable lineage effects from spatial microenvironment effects on tumor cell expression in spatial lineage tracing data. PRNODE extends this partitioning to yeast, jointly estimating mother and daughter protein regulatory networks to quantify inheritance. SpaDAG learns spatially varying causal DAGs in spatial transcriptomics via MCMC, and an ABC, sequential Monte Carlo and random forest pipeline ranks parameters in agent-based tumor models. The emphasis is on separating inherited from environmental contributions and on reporting ambiguity rather than a single reconstruction.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
